  "vulnerability_information": "At `lib/ws.c:1734`, `ws_flush()` borrows a pointer from the outgoing `sendbuf` and passes it to `ws_send_raw_blocking()`; it skips those bytes only after the send returns. A `curl_ws_send()` from the WebSocket write callback can be interrupted by a TCP-trace debug callback that calls `curl_ws_send()` again, and the nested flush frees the chunk the outer send is using. On `curl-8_23_0` with `ENABLE_DEBUG=OFF`, ASan reports a 32,767-byte use-after-free read in `send()`, while the no-nested control is clean. In a Release run, the first decoded frame differs at byte 32,754, a duplicate frame header appears inside it at raw offset 32,768, and 32,767 bytes from a test allocation that reused the freed chunk reach the server in the raw tail. This path does not use `curl_easy_pause()` and survives the proposed fixes for my earlier reports.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. ASan build, nested trigger, and no-nested control:\n\n   ```sh\n   POC=/absolute/path/to/h1-attachments\n   git checkout curl-8_23_0\n   cmake -S . -B bld-asan -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DBUILD_STATIC_LIBS=ON -DENABLE_DEBUG=OFF -DCURL_DISABLE_VERBOSE_STRINGS=OFF -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=\"-fsanitize=address -fno-omit-frame-pointer -g\"\n   cmake --build bld-asan --target libcurl_static -j2\n   sh \"$POC/run.sh\" \"$PWD/bld-asan\" nested   # UAF, READ of size 32767\n   sh \"$POC/run.sh\" \"$PWD/bld-asan\" control  # CLEAN\n   ```\n\n2. Release build, canary, and control:\n\n   ```sh\n   cmake -S . -B bld-release -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DBUILD_STATIC_LIBS=ON -DENABLE_DEBUG=OFF -DCURL_DISABLE_VERBOSE_STRINGS=OFF\n   cmake --build bld-release --target libcurl_static -j2\n   sh \"$POC/run.sh\" \"$PWD/bld-release\" canary   # CORRUPT, 32767-byte 0xA5 run\n   sh \"$POC/run.sh\" \"$PWD/bld-release\" control  # CLEAN\n   ```\n\n3. Fixed control and regression test:\n\n   ```sh\n   git apply \"$POC/ws-send-fix-and-test.diff\"\n   cmake --build bld-asan --target libcurl_static -j2\n   sh \"$POC/run.sh\" \"$PWD/bld-asan\" nested   # CLEAN\n   ```\n\n   Test 2313 in the diff fails before the fix and passes after it.\n\nSource history points to commit 02edae54e8, first included in 8.12.0; the earliest release where I reproduced the UAF is 8.15.0, while 8.10.0 was clean. I did not run 8.12.0.\n\n## Impact\n\nA WebSocket peer can receive bytes from reused heap memory when an application uses this nested callback pattern",
